00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:29.740
MARK MANDEL: So now
it's far, far simpler.

00:02:29.740 --> 00:02:32.800
Simply put, if you are
going to write something,

00:02:32.800 --> 00:02:35.582
it is simply based on that
write for that entity.

00:02:35.582 --> 00:02:37.790
You no longer have to worry
about indexes or anything

00:02:37.790 --> 00:02:38.650
like that.

00:02:38.650 --> 00:02:39.430
Reads it the same.

00:02:39.430 --> 00:02:41.740
The cost is per entity.

00:02:41.740 --> 00:02:45.050
And deletes are exactly the same
in that it's just per entity.

00:02:45.050 --> 00:02:48.424
You'll be charged for a single
delete operation per entity,

00:02:48.424 --> 00:02:50.340
and we've got flat rates
for all of those now.

00:02:50.340 --> 00:02:54.040
So for you to work out exactly
what those sort of costs

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:56.410
