00:06:00.140 --> 00:06:02.556
JUSTIN BECKWITH: Yeah, so there
are a lot of great reasons

00:06:02.556 --> 00:06:03.350
to use Node.js.

00:06:03.350 --> 00:06:05.250
I think the big thing
that first attracted me

00:06:05.250 --> 00:06:06.958
to the platform and
the first development

00:06:06.958 --> 00:06:08.870
team I was on that
started using it,

00:06:08.870 --> 00:06:11.350
it was about taking advantage
of a single language

00:06:11.350 --> 00:06:13.550
both for our front end
and our back end code.

00:06:13.550 --> 00:06:15.670
So we had spent years
and years and years

00:06:15.670 --> 00:06:17.730
building up this--
building up a lot of muscle

00:06:17.730 --> 00:06:20.610
on using JavaScript for
front end web applications.

00:06:20.610 --> 00:06:22.420
And all of a sudden
you go to the back end

00:06:22.420 --> 00:06:24.420
and you had to go completely
different language,

00:06:24.420 --> 00:06:25.920
different package
manager, different

00:06:25.920 --> 00:06:28.440
build system, different
libraries, the whole thing.

00:06:28.440 --> 00:06:30.070
I think the big
beauty of Node.js

00:06:30.070 --> 00:06:32.680
is that you learn one
language, one ecosystem.

00:06:32.680 --> 00:06:34.700
You know, npm is getting huge.

00:06:34.700 --> 00:06:36.800
